      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5fdfed009a58a3291ed998d9",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've noticed recently due to a few events that when a user blocks me within one of my own worlds two things happen:\n1: They vanish from the Social List and are nearly impossible to track down quickly making it hard to moderate Malicious Users. I've not been able to track them down using the method of selecting a user and clicking the next button, instead I must know their name and find them through the Search Function on the social tab. By the time I can find them, if I have their name, it will usually be too late and people have been crashed.\n2: A User can Block and then Unblock you causing the UI to not show them in the world but still allowing them to use malicious avatars that could freeze the use of the UI or crash you if your safety settings are not set up. All they would need to do then is keep a broken line of sight from the host.\nI would like to be able as the Host/Creator of a world to see all users within an instance and be able to moderate them in case someone purposefully blocks the host with the intent to handicap their ability to remove and report users with ill intent. There have been several instances where a user will scout the room first and block me or I am asked to come remove a crasher or harassing player from a room but I am unable to due to the fact they block me first or the off chance I have blocked them prior.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
